   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\"><span class=\"kind\">function</span> IgnoreCriticalExtension <span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Cryptography.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CRYPT_50119\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Cryptography.pdf)\">[SWS_CRYPT_50119]</a></span> <span class=\"ups\">Upstream: <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_Cryptography.pdf#nameddest=RS_CRYPTO_02306\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_Cryptography.pdf)\">RS_CRYPTO_02306</a></span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">virtual <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_Result_d51722.html\">ara::core::Result</a>&lt; void &gt; IgnoreCriticalExtension (<a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_StringView_cfeb8f.html\">ara::core::StringView</a> ignoredExtensionOid) noexcept=0;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Configure the context to ignore an extension during validation of certificates and OCSP responses, even if the extension is marked as critical and the validation context does not support the extension. It is the responsibility of the application to validate such extensions. Multiple invocations of this function lead to ignoring all passed extensions. This function has no effect if the kIgnoreUnknownCriticalExtensions validation option is set.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
